{
  "id": "phase-073",
  "title": "Measure before optimizing: a benchmark harness with a checked-in baseline",
  "severity": "major",
  "depends_on": [
    "phase-107"
  ],
  "risk": "medium",
  "finding": "Redblue has no benchmark harness at all: no `benches/` or `benchmarks/` directory exists, `Cargo.toml` names no criterion/divan dependency, and no BASELINE file records how fast anything is. Ipp ships `benchmarks/run_benchmarks.py` plus a checked-in `BENCHMARKS.md` table (fibonacci, prime counting, mandelbrot, string concat across interpreter/VM/Python/Node) for exactly this reason \u2014 and phase-022's 29.0s-to-3.5s speedup claim had nowhere to live except a FINDINGS paragraph, so no later phase can tell whether it regressed. Performance work without a harness is unmeasurable by construction.",
  "goal": "Add a benchmark harness (named workloads: fibonacci, prime counting, string concat, lex-heavy compile) that prints a timing table and records it in a checked-in `BENCH.md`, with every workload asserting the CORRECTNESS of its output (fib(20)==6765 etc. \u2014 deterministic, never flaky). Wall time is printed and recorded but never asserted: timing assertions are flakes wearing a gate's clothes.",
  "must_touch": [
    "tests/"
  ],
  "accept": [
    "four named workloads run to completion and print one table with per-workload wall time (asserted present in output, never asserted exact)",
    "every workload asserts its computed answer against a literal (fib(20) is 6765, the prime count is exact, the concat is exact) \u2014 a benchmark that computes the wrong answer fast is the failure this pins",
    "`BENCH.md` is checked in with the measured table from the landing machine plus its hardware note, and a test asserts the file exists and names all four workloads (content may move, coverage may not)",
    "the harness runs outside the `cargo test` gate path (it measures, it does not gate) while its correctness assertions run inside it \u2014 one mechanism never serves both masters",
    "edge_* tests cover an empty workload name (clean usage error listing the four), a workload given a size of zero (completes, answer asserted trivially true), and a 60-second budget the harness enforces itself (a hung workload fails loudly instead of hanging CI)"
  ],
  "timeout_min": 120
}
