All findings fixed:

- Added a hidden sleeping worker and `edge_a_hung_child_process_is_killed_at_its_budget`, which drives `run_workload` through the real child path, asserts `BudgetExceeded`, and proves no child survives its finish marker.
- Unit-tested every `parse_worker_output` branch (`ERR`, bad field count, bad nanos, bad number hex, unknown tag, non-UTF-8, odd/invalid hex).
- `measure_in_child` now kills the child on the read-error branch too; `DEFAULT_BUDGET` docs match the child-process design.
- Baseline parsing now rejects misspelled workloads even with malformed sizes; `--compare` refuses a baseline missing any of the four workloads.
- Report gate counts corrected to the observed output and synced to the pipeline report.

